# LibreWolf r8-keep-rules.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M6-07 ("Make the R8-minified release build actually boot")
#
# THE CRASH (reproduced, logcat saved)
# -----------------------------------
# Every R8-minified release build of the Android port dies on launch:
#
#   FATAL EXCEPTION: main
#   java.lang.Error: Structure.getFieldOrder() on class
#       org.mozilla.experiments.nimbus.internal.RustBuffer$ByValue
#       does not provide enough names [0] ([]) to match declared fields
#       [3] ([capacity, data, len])
#       at com.sun.jna.Structure.getFields(r8-map-id-7758...:144)
#
# Evidence from the LW-M4-09 build (same tree, same crash):
#   ~/lw-m4-09/apk-patched/fenix-x86_64-release.apk          (R8 on, crashes)
#   ~/lw-m4-09/apk-patched-noopt/fenix-x86_64-release.apk    (R8 off, boots)
#   ~/lw-m4-09/evidence/release-r8-crash.logcat              (the crash above)
#
# ROOT CAUSE (verified against the ESR tarball and the built AAR)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# It is NOT "R8 renames the JNA fields". R8 strips the
# @com.sun.jna.Structure.FieldOrder RUNTIME annotation from the uniffi-
# generated RustBuffer classes (third_party/rust/uniffi_bindgen/src/bindings/
# kotlin/templates/RustBufferTemplate.kt, which declares
# @Structure.FieldOrder("capacity", "len", "data") on capacity/len/data).
# com.sun.jna.Structure.getFieldOrder() reads that annotation at runtime and
# gets back an empty name list, so the "enough names [0] ([]) to match
# declared fields [3]" Error fires the moment the Nimbus FFI is touched.
#
# The keep rules that Mozilla ships for exactly this are delivered through the
# application-services AAR's consumer ProGuard file. The build already
# references it:
#
#   third_party/application-services/build-scripts/
#   component-common.gradle (release block):
#       consumerProguardFiles \
#           "$appServicesRootDir/proguard-rules-consumer-jna.pro"
#
# but that file is ABSENT from the Firefox source tarball. Verified on
# firefox-153.0esr.source.tar.xz (the base this board builds):
#
#   $ tar -tJf firefox-153.0esr.source.tar.xz | grep application-services
#   .../third_party/application-services/build-scripts/component-common.gradle
#   (no proguard-rules-consumer-jna.pro anywhere in the tarball)
#
# so the in-tree-built Nimbus AAR ships with NO consumer ProGuard rules.
# Verified in a built AAR (LW-M2-04 batch tree): META-INF/ contains only
# com/android/build/gradle/aar-metadata.properties -- no
# proguard.txt. Consequence: in fenix:assembleRelease, R8 runs against the
# Nimbus AAR with only fenix/app/proguard-rules.pro (which keeps
# mozilla.appservices.** but NOT org.mozilla.experiments.nimbus.internal.**),
# the annotation is stripped, and the app dies on the first RustBuffer use.
# The only "release" APKs ever built by this project were therefore built
# with -PdisableOptimization (R8 off) -- which is why LW-M4-09's booting
# APK lives in apk-patched-noopt/.
#
# THE FIX
# -------
# Restore the file the build already points at. The content below is
# byte-identical to upstream Mozilla's
# proguard-rules-consumer-jna.pro (fetched 2026-08-20 from
# github.com/mozilla/application-services main, 949 bytes). Its two jobs:
#
#   * -keepattributes ...RuntimeVisibleAnnotations... -- R8 may drop runtime
#     annotations without them; the @Structure.FieldOrder annotation is what
#     Structure.getFieldOrder() needs.
#   * -keep class org.mozilla.experiments.nimbus.internal.** { *; } --
#     stops R8 from renaming/merging the uniffi FFI classes (RustBuffer and
#     friends) that the Rust side addresses by name.
#   * the JNA rules -- JNA resolves field layout from the annotation and
#     the class shape; upstream keeps all of it.
#
# Why this path is Android-only (android.txt, not common.txt):
#   * third_party/application-services/ is shared source, but this file is a
#     pure Gradle BUILD INPUT (consumerProguardFiles of the AAR's release
#     buildType). The desktop build never consumes AAR consumer rules; the
#     file is dead weight but harmless there. Keeping it in android.txt means
#     the desktop tree stays byte-identical to stock -- the stronger guarantee.
#   * scripts/lint-patch-scope.py for android.txt only forbids browser/
#     paths; this one is clean.
#
# Ordering: touches a file no other patch in any list touches (checked
# against common.txt and android.txt), so it has no ordering constraint.
# Applied to a pristine 153.0esr tree with zero fuzz by
# scripts/check-patchfail.sh --targets=android.
#
# WHAT THIS UNLOCKS
# -----------------
# fenix:assembleRelease with minifyEnabled=true (R8 on) for the first time.
# scripts/android-apk.sh gains a release variant in the same change (LW-M6-07).
# The acceptance bar is a logcat of the R8-minified release APK loading a page
# with no FATAL EXCEPTION, plus scripts/android-smoke.sh --check-no-gms green
# on that same release APK -- not "the keep rules look right".

--- /dev/null
+++ b/third_party/application-services/proguard-rules-consumer-jna.pro
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# ProGuard rules for consumers of this library.
+
+# JNA specific rules
+# See https://github.com/java-native-access/jna/blob/master/www/FrequentlyAskedQuestions.md#jna-on-android
+-dontwarn java.awt.*
+-keep class com.sun.jna.* { *; }
+-keep class * extends com.sun.jna.* { *; }
+-keepclassmembers class * extends com.sun.jna.* { public *; }
+
+####################################################################################################
+# Add explicit keep rules for Nimbus RustBuffer and related structs to avoid
+# overly-aggressive optimization when R8 fullMode is enabled, leading to crashes.
+####################################################################################################
+-keepattributes RuntimeVisibleAnnotations,RuntimeInvisibleAnnotations,RuntimeVisibleTypeAnnotations,RuntimeInvisibleTypeAnnotations,AnnotationDefault,InnerClasses,EnclosingMethod,Signature
+-keep class org.mozilla.experiments.nimbus.internal.** { *; }
